      "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution to a Trigonometric Equation Containing Sine or Cosine",
      "problem": "What is the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=1?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nThe sine function has a period of $2\\pi .$ Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .\n$$",
