      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Coordinates of the Points of Intersection of a Trigonometric Curve and a Horizontal Line",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/350458d29c8d214f44b175e28a6f43accd7ce064187cf755324cbe99d53eb7ad.png)\n\nThe graph shows a portion of the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and $y=-1.$ Which of the following generates the $x$-values of all of their points of intersection? Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
      "worked_solution": "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-1.$ \n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of $\\pi .$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\n$$",
